'\" t
.TH NINITCTL 8 2026-09-30 "ninit @PACKAGE_VERSION@"
.SH NAME
ninitctl \- compile, inspect and control the ninit service graph
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ninitctl init
.RB [ \-d
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-check ]
.br
.B ninitctl show
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [[ \-f ]
.IR file ]
.br
.B ninitctl add
.RB [ \-d
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\- ]
.IR name ...
.br
.B ninitctl del
.RB [ \-d
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\- ]
.IR name ...
.br
.B ninitctl status
.RI [ name ]
.br
.B ninitctl log
.RB [ \-e ]
.RB [ \-w ]
.br
.BR "ninitctl start" | stop | restart
.I name
.br
.B ninitctl resume
.br
.B ninitctl help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ninitctl
compiles the service directory described in
.BR ninit.d (5)
into the graph that
.BR ninit (8)
loads at boot, prints that graph, moves services in and out of use, and sends commands to the running
.BR ninit .
.PP
.BR init ,
.BR show ,
.B add
and
.B del
operate on files and do not require
.B ninit
to be running.
the other commands connect to
.IR /run/ninit/control ,
which only root can open
.SH CONFIGURATION COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
compile the service directory and write the graph.
the steps are:
.RS
.IP 1. 4
take an exclusive
.BR flock (2)
on the service directory, the same lock
.B add
and
.B del
take
.IP 2. 4
parse every service file and strip the comments from its script, when the interpreter lexes like sh, see
.BR ninit.d (5).
the first error ends the command
.IP 3. 4
check every stripped script with
.BR "@ninit_shell@ \-n" ,
up to 32 in parallel, and report every syntax error.
bash checks with
.B extglob
on
.IP 4. 4
resolve dependencies and reject unknown names, self dependencies and cycles
.IP 5. 4
order the services topologically, placing services without prerequisites first, then the service with the longest chain of dependents, then by name
.IP 6. 4
resolve the default
.B onfail
of each service
.IP 7. 4
verify the result with the checks
.B ninit
applies at boot
.IP 8. 4
write it to a temporary file and
.BR fsync (2)
it, link the existing graph to
.IB file .old\c
, rename the temporary file to
.IR file ,
and
.BR fsync (2)
the directory
.RE
.IP
nothing is written if any step fails, and an existing
.I file
or
.IB file .old
that is not a graph is never replaced.
the graph has mode 0644, less group or other read permission if any service file lacks it, less the umask.
.B init
warns about daemons that have dependents and no
.BR notify ,
about a missing or empty
.IR /etc/locale.conf ,
about a
.B #!\&
line naming another interpreter, and about directives after the header
.TP
.B show
verify a graph and print it as a table, followed by one of its longest dependency chains
.TP
.B add
move each
.IR dir /unused/ name
to
.IR dir / name
.TP
.B del
move each
.IR dir / name
to
.IR dir /unused/ name ,
creating
.IR dir /unused
if needed
.PP
.B add
and
.B del
never replace an existing file.
a relative symbolic link is rewritten to resolve to the same target from its new location.
neither command rebuilds the graph
.SH RUNTIME COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
print the state of every service, or of
.I name
.TP
.B log
print the log ring of
.BR ninit ,
oldest first
.TP
.B start
clear the hold on
.IR name ,
reset its start attempts and restart delay, and start it.
the command returns when the service is ready or has failed, and fails if neither happens within its
.B start-timeout
plus 2 s.
it is refused if the service is running or its previous instance has not exited.
if a prerequisite is not up it is refused, and the service is left pending to start when its prerequisites are up.
a oneshot that has completed is run again
.TP
.B stop
hold
.IR name ,
send it
.BR SIGTERM ,
and send
.B SIGKILL
when its
.B stop-timeout
expires.
the command returns when the service has stopped, and fails if it has not stopped 2 s after
.BR SIGKILL .
dependents are not stopped
.TP
.B restart
.B stop
then
.BR start ,
or
.B start
alone if
.I name
is already stopped
.TP
.B resume
return every failed and skipped service to pending, reset its start attempts, and start each whose prerequisites are up
.TP
.B help
print a summary of the commands
.PP
a held service is not restarted, not started when its prerequisites come up, and not started by
.BR resume .
a service accepts one operation at a time.
targets cannot be started, stopped or restarted.
an operation continues if
.B ninitctl
is interrupted
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir " \fIdir\fR"
service directory.
default
.I @ninit_svcdir@
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-out " \fIfile\fR"
output of
.BR init .
default
.IR dir /depgraph
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " \fIfile\fR"
graph read by
.BR show .
default
.I @ninit_svcdir@/depgraph
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
perform every step of
.B init
except writing the output
.TP
.B \-\-no\-check
skip the syntax check of
.B init
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
with
.BR show ,
print under each service its effective timeouts, start attempts, start delay and
.B deps
mode, marked
.B (set)
if the file sets any of them and
.B (default)
otherwise, followed by its script as stored, without comments
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-error
with
.BR log ,
print only
.B WARN
and
.B FAIL
lines
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-watch
with
.BR log ,
then print each line as it is logged, until interrupted.
lines overwritten before they are read are replaced by one
.B WARN
line,
.BI "log: skipped " n " bytes"
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
print a summary of the commands
.SH OUTPUT
the columns of
.B show
are:
.TP
.B #
index in the graph, which also names the service's cgroup,
.BI svc\- #
.TP
.B service
service name
.TP
.B type
.BR oneshot ,
.B daemon
or
.B target
.TP
.B lvl
number of services in the longest prerequisite chain ending at the service, the service included
.TP
.B kills
number of services that depend on the service directly or indirectly, which are skipped if it fails
.TP
.B onfail
effective failure policy
.TP
.B rdy
notify descriptor
.TP
.B rst
.B yes
if the service has
.B restart: always
.TP
.B depends on
direct prerequisites
.PP
the columns of
.B status
are index, name, state and main process id, and
.B held
when any service is held.
the states are:
.TP
.B pending
not started, or stopped before it became ready
.TP
.B starting
spawned and not yet ready
.TP
.B up
ready and still up
.TP
.B down
was ready and has since exited or been stopped
.TP
.B failed
exhausted its start attempts
.TP
.B skipped
not started because a prerequisite failed or went down
.PP
output to a terminal is coloured
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
success
.TP
.B 1
failure, including a failure reported by
.B ninit
and an unreachable control socket
.TP
.B 2
usage error
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @ninit_svcdir@
service directory
.TP
.I @ninit_svcdir@/unused
disabled services
.TP
.I @ninit_svcdir@/depgraph
compiled graph
.TP
.I @ninit_svcdir@/depgraph.old
graph replaced by the last
.B init
.TP
.I /run/ninit/control
control socket
.SH EXAMPLES
check the service directory without writing anything, then compile it:
.PP
.EX
ninitctl init \-n
ninitctl init
.EE
.PP
disable a service and rebuild:
.PP
.EX
ninitctl del sshd
ninitctl init
.EE
.PP
retry everything that failed during boot:
.PP
.EX
ninitctl log \-e
ninitctl resume
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ninit (8),
.BR ninit.d (5),
.BR ninit\-shutdown (8)
